# Scripted history of the sample legacy repository, replayed by com.archaeologist.sample.SampleRepository.
#
# A small order system in the style of Java 6/7, with the signals the agent looks for:
# - OrderManager is the hotspot: a god class changed by every author, with most of the bug fixes;
# - TaxCalculator is complex but stable: written once, fixed once;
# - Messages is simple but changed often, and is encoded in ISO-8859-1, as old projects often were;
# - util/DateHelper is renamed to common/DateUtils, and changed before and after;
# - two bulk commits touch every source file (license header, company rename);
# - bug fixes in English and Portuguese, issue keys (SHOP-123) and vague messages ("ajustes", "wip");
# - JDBC, java.util.Date, Random, a static singleton, reflection and file I/O;
# - an interface, a generated class, one JUnit 4 test, a .mailmap and a file with CRLF line endings.
# All authors are fictional and use addresses at reserved example domains.
#
# Format:
#   author <key>: <Name> <<e-mail>>
#   file <path>: encoding <charset> | line-endings CRLF
#   commit <days before today> <author key>, then the message on the next line, then operations:
#     add <path>                 content between <<< and >>>
#     replace <path>             <<< old === new >>> (old must occur exactly once)
#     replace-all *.<ext>        <<< old === new >>> (every occurrence, in every such file holding it)
#     prepend *.<ext>            <<< text >>> (to every such file)
#     rename <from> -> <to>

author ana: Ana Souza <ana.souza@example.com>
author ana2: Ana S. <ana@corp.example.com>
author bruno: Bruno Lima <bruno.lima@example.com>
author carla: Carla Mendes <carla@example.com>
author diego: Diego Rocha <diego.rocha@example.org>
author eva: Eva Martins <eva@example.net>

file src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Messages.java: encoding ISO-8859-1
file src/main/java/com/acme/shop/ReportGenerator.java: line-endings CRLF

